      ],
      "source": "https://www.lewistonmaine.gov/421/History-of-Lewiston",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Lewiston’s canal construction in 1850 drew about 400 Irish workers and later Québécois millworkers, shaping its labor history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lewiston%2C_Maine",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Maine Museum of Innovation, Learning and Labor sits in a former textile factory, preserving the city’s manufacturing legacy.",
